From 7737f1bff4adb031b01dd9108b5a8f0746821748 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:31:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 106/110] Skills:  training speed, all skills for new
 characters, /queue

New settings in eve-server.xml <character>:
- skillTrainingSpeed:  a multiplier on skill points per minute (1.0 is
  Tranquility's speed, 10.0 the default here)
- injectAllSkills:  new characters get every published skill injected
  at level 0, so there are no skillbooks to buy
- magic14AtFive:  new characters start with the 'magic 14' core skills
  at V
A new character gets the cheapest clone that covers the skill points it
starts with.

/queue lifts the client's 24 hour skill queue limit (the server never
had one):  /queue shows your queue with its real end times, /queue add
<skill> [level] adds a skill (and what it needs first), /queue add
<ship or module> adds everything that needs, and /queue remove <skill>
and /queue clear take them out.  The client is told to fetch the queue
again.

Fixes rolled in:
- untrained skills' levels and skill points load as whole numbers (the
  skill queue window failed on a float)
- logging off while a skill trains no longer crashes the server later
